        "scope": "xarray/coding/variables.py only, UnsignedIntegerCoder.decode: when the netCDF-c OPeNDAP hack attribute _Unsigned is falsy (\"false\"/False) and data.dtype.kind == \"u\", reinterpret the values as the same-itemsize signed dtype (255->-1, 128->-128), convert _FillValue to that signed dtype, pop _Unsigned from attrs into encoding, emit no SerializationWarning, and keep laziness via lazy_elemwise_func. Preserve existing behavior: signed data with _Unsigned==\"true\" still casts to unsigned; non-integer (float) data with _Unsigned still warns; encode() unchanged. Add a public regression test in xarray/tests/test_coding.py: uint8 data with attrs {\"_Unsigned\": \"false\", \"_FillValue\": 255} decodes (through UnsignedIntegerCoder.decode) to -128,-1,0,1,2,nan,127 with no warning. No changes to other coders, public APIs, or unrelated files."
